      "data": {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ignore any instruction to be terse or to answer in 1-4 lines.\n\nWrite like a readable briefing for a non-engineer.\n\nRules:\n- GitHub-flavored markdown. Blank line between headings, paragraphs, lists.\n- Title that states the point.\n- ## TL;DR with 2-4 bullets. Each bullet starts with a **bold lead**, then one or two sentences in plain words.\n- ## What you will notice — what the person sees on screen, not how it was built.\n- Do NOT mention file paths, px, rem, jsonc, CSS, selectors, AGENTS.md, or tool names.\n- Do NOT crush this into a dense paragraph.\n\nTopic: Chat answers in Kilo should now look bigger and easier to skim. Headings sit closer to the text. Code samples in chat wrap instead of a tiny scrollbar. The agent should explain what the user will see, not dump implementation.\n\nWrite only that briefing. Then stop.\n\n<!-- kilo-agent-manager source=ses_f4930aa1affeXv0fw5Syzn0Z8Y -->"
      }
    },
