      "data": {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "# Chat answers now look bigger and easier to skim\n\n## TL;DR\n\n- **Text is larger.** Replies should feel easier to read at a glance, not cramped.\n- **Headings sit closer to the words they introduce.** You spend less time hunting for where a section actually starts.\n- **Code samples wrap.** Long lines stay in view instead of hiding behind a tiny side-to-side scrollbar.\n- **Answers talk about what you will see.** The agent should explain the result in plain words, not dump how it was built.\n\n## What you will notice\n\nChat replies should feel more like a short briefing than a wall of tiny text.\n\nHeadings and the paragraphs under them look like they belong together. You should be able to scan a title, then drop straight into the next sentence without a big empty gap.\n\nWhen the answer includes a code sample, long lines wrap onto the next line. You should not have to drag a thin scrollbar just to read the rest of a line.\n\nThe writing itself should tell you what changed on screen. You should see the outcome in everyday language, not a pile of build details.",
        "time": {
          "start": 1789872953747,
          "end": 1789872957947
        }
      }
